{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '672,711p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '920,993p' task/evaluate_final.py; jq '{keys:keys,manifest_first:(.files[0]|{case,seed,profile,sizes,lineage}),file_count:(.files|length)}' task/resources/final/manifest.json; sed -n '155,217p' results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_tail_adaptive_residual_scaling/program_1/src/program.py; sed -n '1,60p' .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"keys\": [\n    \"aggregation\",\n    \"canonicalization\",\n    \"controls\",\n    \"cross_plane_check\",\n    \"environment\",\n    \"files\",\n    \"generator_description\",\n    \"generator_license\",\n    \"limitations\",\n    \"normalization\",\n    \"operation_table\",\n    \"production_seeds\",\n    \"schema_version\",\n    \"smoke_seeds\"\n  ],\n  \"manifest_first\": {\n    \"case\": \"H3\",\n    \"seed\": 1009,\n    \"profile\": \"production\",\n    \"sizes\": [\n      1024,\n      1024,\n      512,\n      2048\n    ],\n    \"lineage\": [\n      991,\n      1009,\n      0,\n      0,\n      121\n    ]\n  },\n  \"file_count\": 42\n}\n    mean, deviation, coefficients = model\n    return np.clip(features((covariates - mean) / deviation) @ coefficients,\n                   np.log(1e-4), np.log(1e4))\n\n\ndef raw_candidate_logs(incumbent, tail_model, covariates):\n    incumbent_log_scale = predict_incumbent_log(incumbent, covariates)\n    tail_log_scale = predict_quantile_stumps(tail_model, covariates)\n    return np.column_stack((incumbent_log_scale, np.zeros(len(covariates)),\n                            *(blend_log_scales(incumbent_log_scale, tail_log_scale, weight)\n                              for weight in (0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0))))\n\n\ndef align_log_scale(log_norms, fitted_log_scale, quantile):\n    alignment_offset = float(np.quantile(log_norms - fitted_log_scale, quantile))\n    return alignment_offset\n\n\ndef fit_scale_family(covariates, residual_norms, log_norms, tail_model, quantile):\n    incumbent = fit_incumbent(covariates, residual_norms)\n    fitted_candidates = raw_candidate_logs(incumbent, tail_model, covariates)\n    offsets = np.asarray([align_log_scale(log_norms, fitted_candidates[:, index], quantile)\n                          for index in range(fitted_candidates.shape[1])])\n    return dict(incumbent=incumbent, tail=tail_model, alignment_offsets=offsets)\n\n\ndef fit_scale(features, residual_norms):\n    quantile, max_rounds = 0.9, 80\n    log_norms = np.log(np.maximum(residual_norms, 1e-12))\n    selected_index = 0\n    if len(log_norms) >= 3:\n        indices = np.random.default_rng(0).permutation(len(log_norms))\n        folds = np.array_split(indices, 3)\n        fold_losses = []\n        for fold_index, validation_indices in enumerate(folds):\n            fit_indices = np.concatenate([fold for index, fold in enumerate(folds)\n                                          if index != fold_index])\n            assert np.intersect1d(fit_indices, validation_indices).size == 0\n            min_leaf = max(20, math.ceil(0.03 * len(fit_indices)))\n            fold_tail_model = fit_quantile_stumps(features[fit_indices], log_norms[fit_indices], quantile, max_rounds, min_leaf)\n            family = fit_scale_family(features[fit_indices], residual_norms[fit_indices],\n                                      log_norms[fit_indices], fold_tail_model, quantile)\n            held_out = raw_candidate_logs(family['incumbent'], family['tail'],\n                                          features[validation_indices])\n            held_out += family['alignment_offsets']\n            fold_losses.append(pinball_loss(log_norms[validation_indices, None],\n                                            held_out, quantile).mean(axis=0))\n        fold_losses = np.asarray(fold_losses)\n        mean_losses = fold_losses.mean(axis=0)\n        standard_errors = fold_losses.std(axis=0, ddof=1) / np.sqrt(len(folds))\n        best_index = int(np.argmin(mean_losses))\n        selection_limit = mean_losses[best_index] + standard_errors[best_index]\n        simplicity_order = (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5)\n        selected_index = next(index for index in simplicity_order if mean_losses[index] <= selection_limit)\n    min_leaf = max(20, math.ceil(0.03 * len(log_norms)))\n    tail_model = fit_quantile_stumps(features, log_norms, quantile, max_rounds, min_leaf)\n    model = fit_scale_family(features, residual_norms, log_norms, tail_model, quantile)\n    model['selected_index'] = selected_index\n    return model\n\n\ndef predict_scale(model, covariates):\n    selected_index = model['selected_index']\n---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evaluations, failures, and next hypotheses during agent runs.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nKeep durable run memory so idea evolution and program evidence are never lost between steps.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- At run start to initialize memory.\n- After every meaningful step (`idea`, `edit`, `evaluate`, `verify`, `paper`, `draft`).\n- Immediately after every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair.\n\n# What to do\n1. Initialize `./memory.md` if missing with these section headers:\n- `# Memory Log`\n- `## Context`\n- `## Idea Discoveries`\n- `## Program Evaluations`\n- `## Failures / Regressions`\n- `## Next Hypotheses`\n2. Also initialize global files if missing:\n- `./global_memory/memory.md`\n- `./global_memory/memory.jsonl`\n3. Never delete or rewrite prior entries; append only.\n4. For each appended entry, include:\n- timestamp\n- step type\n- change/discovery summary\n- concrete evidence\n- next action\n5. After every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair, append a `Program Evaluations` entry that includes:\n- `program_<idx>`\n- `combined_score`\n- `correct`\n- rubric pass/fail summary\n- `next_recommendation`\n6. For regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly\nto the required markdown and JSONL files. Preserve all existing content. When command\nexecution is available, prefer the helper for deterministic dual-write:\n- script: detect the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\nMEMORY_HELPER=\"$(find ./.claude ./.codex ./.cursor ./.opencode ./.gemini ./.pi -path '*/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py' -print -quit 2>/dev/null)\"\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" \\\n  --global-memory-md \"./global_memory/memory.md\" \\\n  --global-memory-jsonl \"./global_memory/memory.jsonl\" \\\n  --event-json '{\"step\":\"evaluate\",\"scope\":\"attempt\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"evidence\":\"...\",\"next_action\":\"...\",\"attempt_id\":\"{{ATTEMPT_ID}}\",\"idea_id\":\"{{IDEA_ID}}\",\"program_id\":\"program_2\",\"metrics\":{\"combined_score\":2.54,\"correct\":true}}'\n```\n9. JSONL event schema (required keys):\n- `timestamp` (auto-filled if omitted)\n- `step` (`idea|edit|evaluate|verify|paper|draft|final|conclusions_skip`)\n- `scope` (`idea|attempt|paper|campaign`)\n- `summary`\n- `evidence`\n- `next_action`\n- optional: `idea_id`, `attempt_id`, `program_id`, `metrics`, `rubrics`, `tags`\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
