{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'def .*context|probe|train|sizes|groups|ridge|reference|bootstrap|draws|percentile|quantile|seeds =' task/evaluate_final.py | tail -75; sed -n '718,796p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '961,993p' task/evaluate_final.py; jq -c '{seed_values:([.files[].seed]|unique),sizes:([.files[]|select(.profile==\\\"production\\\")|.sizes]|unique),keys:keys}' task/resources/final/manifest.json; sed -n '1,70p' task/program_0/src/program.py; cat .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'def .*context|probe|train|sizes|groups|ridge|reference|bootstrap|draws|percentile|quantile|seeds =' task/evaluate_final.py | tail -75; sed -n '718,796p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '961,993p' task/evaluate_final.py; jq -c '{seed_values:([.files[].seed]|unique),sizes:([.files[]|select(.profile==\\\"production\\\")|.sizes]|unique),keys:keys}' task/resources/final/manifest.json; sed -n '1,70p' task/program_0/src/program.py; cat .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"{\"seed_values\":[1009,2003,3001,4001,5003,6007],\"sizes\":[[1024,1024,512,2048]],\"keys\":[\"aggregation\",\"canonicalization\",\"controls\",\"cross_plane_check\",\"environment\",\"files\",\"generator_description\",\"generator_license\",\"limitations\",\"normalization\",\"operation_table\",\"production_seeds\",\"schema_version\",\"smoke_seeds\"]}\n\"\"\"Train-only positive compositional residual-scale learner, python_rpc_v1:handle.\n\nAll requests/responses are finite JSON objects; extra response keys are forbidden.\nreset: {op:'reset', seed: nonnegative int} -> {ok:true}. Clears all model/transfer\nstate. Any seed is accepted; seeds initialize randomness, never select a workload.\nfit: {op:'fit', x:Array[n,6], residuals:Array[n], dimension:int>=2,\n      scale_min:0.0001, scale_max:10000.0} -> {ok:true}.\nOnly training covariates and training residual norms are provided. Fits replace the\nmodel. Prediction is read-only and requires a completed fit after reset.\npredict: {op:'predict', x:Array[n,6]} -> {scales:Array[n]}.\nReturn strictly positive finite scales; the evaluator consistently clips them to\n[0.0001,10000]. No calibration/test outcomes or later scoring feedback is given.\nArray is exactly {encoding:'base64',dtype:'<f8',shape:[...],nbytes:int,data:str}.\nData is C-order little-endian float64, n<=2048 normally; no file paths are used.\nWorkload dimensions/settings come from fit, not reset seeds. Candidate changes may\nchange the scale estimator but not evaluator-owned center, geometry or calibration.\n\nOptional bounded fallback, exercised by maximum-protocol tests, not needed for\nordinary shapes: begin {op:'begin',method:'fit'|'predict',fields:object,\narrays:{name:{shape:list,nbytes:int}},nbytes:int} -> {token:str}.\nfields holds the non-array logical request fields except op. Arrays, in insertion\norder, concatenate raw <f8 bytes; total <=8 MiB. upload {op:'upload',token:str,\noffset:int,data:base64str} -> {ok:true}, sequential <=2 chunks of <=4 MiB.\ncommit {op:'commit',token:str} -> {ok:true} validates lengths and computes once.\nexport_start {op:'export_start',token:str} -> {nbytes:int,chunks:int}.\nfetch {op:'fetch',token:str,index:int} -> {data:base64str}, sequential <=2 chunks.\nOutput is UTF-8 JSON for fit, raw <f8 scales for predict. release\n{op:'release',token:str} -> {ok:true} destroys buffers. One live token, <=32 MiB\ntransfer storage; reset invalidates it. No token is a path. At most 8 calls per\nlogical operation (begin,2 uploads,commit,export_start,2 fetches,release).\nNo self-reported learning, timing or diagnostics are accepted as scientific evidence.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport json\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\n\nMODEL = None\nTRANSFER = None\nCHUNK = 4 * 1024 * 1024\n\n\ndef decode(value):\n    if set(value) != {'encoding', 'dtype', 'shape', 'nbytes', 'data'}:\n        raise ValueError('array schema')\n    if value['encoding'] != 'base64' or value['dtype'] != '<f8':\n        raise ValueError('array encoding')\n    raw = base64.b64decode(value['data'], validate=True)\n    if len(raw) != value['nbytes'] or len(raw) != math.prod(value['shape']) * 8:\n        raise ValueError('array size')\n    result = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype='<f8').reshape(value['shape'])\n    if not np.isfinite(result).all():\n        raise ValueError('nonfinite input')\n    return result\n\n\ndef encode(array):\n    array = np.asarray(array, dtype='<f8', order='C')\n    return dict(encoding='base64', dtype='<f8', shape=list(array.shape),\n                nbytes=array.nbytes, data=base64.b64encode(array.tobytes()).decode('ascii'))\n\n\ndef features(array):\n    return np.column_stack((np.ones(len(array)), array, array * array))\n\n\ndef compute(method, fields, arrays):\n    global MODEL\n    if method == 'fit':\n        covariates, residuals = arrays['x'], arrays['residuals']\n---\nname: write-paper-standalone\ndescription: Write a grounded LaTeX paper as one coherent standalone scientific study centered on a single defensible thesis rather than the run chronology.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nGenerate `paper.tex` and `claims_grounding.json` from grounded artifacts only, with a clean standalone-paper narrative.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final paper step when the default paper-writing skill keeps drifting into a search diary.\n- Need a standalone scientific paper built around one central method, hypothesis, or comparison story.\n- Need to hide run order and expose only the subset of baselines and ablations that support a coherent grounded manuscript.\n\n# What to do\n1. Read:\n- `results_readme.md` — campaign-level overview of all tasks, variants, and where to find results. Use this to understand the full scope of the campaign beyond the primary task passed via `--task-dir`.\n- `paper_data.json`\n- `references.bib`\n- `references_provenance.json`\n- `contributions.md` (if provided) — optional base for framing the claimed contributions; not a grounding source\n- `global_memory_summary.md` (if provided)\n- Aggregated CSVs in `/` for fine-grained analysis (install and use pandas) — when available\n- generated figures in `figures/`\n- when `paper_data.json.paper_profile == \"standalone\"`, also follow `presentation_contract` as a visible-language contract\n2. Use `templates/iclr/paper.tex` to keep section order stable. The paper format is **iclr**.\nInspect the selected template and any venue guidance before drafting so the author block, section structure, and framing expectations match the chosen format.\n3. Before drafting, choose one central thesis that is strongly supported by grounded evidence. Do not choose the paper story by recency alone.\n4. Group related implementations into a small number of named method families. Keep only the baseline, proposed method, and ablations needed to support the central thesis.\n5. If the artifacts do not support one coherent paper story, fail clearly instead of narrating the full search process.\n6. Write required sections:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
